WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.330
Speaker 1: Hi, I'm Ferren Cousins in for David
Pakman, and this is the The David Pakman Show

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.590
show, obviously biggest news in the world
right now.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:15.530
We've got to just jump right into this and
that is the deteriorating situation in Afghanistan.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:22.020
Over the weekend, the Afghani president was
forced to evacuate the country, leaving the

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:27.490
capital in Kabul to fall to the Taliban.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:34.400
The Taliban have been encroaching throughout
the country over the last week or so in really

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.000
spectacular fashion, you know, just taking
over as much as they can.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.770
And now it appears with them having seized
the capital, we're in for quite the situation.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:46.770
Right.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.750
And if you've been following social media
over the weekend, I'm sure you've seen plenty

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:55.370
of people with opinions about what should
and should not happen in the country.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.850
Right now.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.180
You've got the corporate controlled media
and, of course, all the Republicans out there

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:06.020
telling us we've got to double down Biden
himself, sending 5000 more troops over the

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:11.569
last week back to Afghanistan when we're supposed
to be getting all of our people out of Afghanistan.

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:15.000
U.S. embassy has had to be evacuated as well.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.409
And then, of course, you have the other side.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.719
You have the people who say, listen, you can't
send anybody over there.

00:01:20.719 --> 00:01:25.159
This is a 20 year, trillion dollar endless
war.

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:28.209
Get the hell out and stay out.

00:01:28.209 --> 00:01:34.009
Unfortunately, it's not as easy as all of
these armchair military strategists would

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:35.319
have you believe.

00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:37.810
It's not as simple as the United States.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.170
Sending thousands of troops over there will
get the Taliban out of the country again and

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.409
everything will be great.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:44.889
Not that simple.

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:49.099
It's not as simple as walking away saying,
oh, well, we created this mess.

00:01:49.099 --> 00:01:51.429
Good luck dealing with it.

00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:55.329
That destabilizes, you know, the region.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:58.189
So what is the answer?

00:01:58.189 --> 00:02:00.079
I don't know.

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:06.639
I don't know, and I'm firmly willing to admit
that I don't know, and I think that's a problem

00:02:06.639 --> 00:02:12.450
that a lot of folks have in this business,
whether it's right or left, always desperate

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.610
to have a definitive answer as to what we
need to do.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.280
And they're always so sure of that answer.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.260
But folks, like I said, I think this is a
situation that's not as black and white as

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.760
a lot of people want to make it seem.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.950
I personally do not want any U.S. troops going
back to Afghanistan.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:36.630
But at the same time, we have to also look
at what we did to that country, we did this.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:40.000
Over 20 years.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.650
We helped to destabilize not just Afghanistan,
but the entire region.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:51.190
With our ridiculous and false foreign policy
based on lies.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.580
And Obama kept us there.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:58.580
Trump acted like he was going to get us out,
you know, tried to negotiate with the Taliban,

00:02:58.580 --> 00:02:59.870
but that didn't do much good.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:05.120
And so Biden comes along and says, well, we're
going to finish getting out of there.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.120
We didn't.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.760
Now we're going back.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.430
So what is the solution you?

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.200
Can we just sit here and say, OK, Taliban,
Afghanistan is yours, we screwed it up, maybe

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.570
you can do better?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.070
I obviously don't think we can do that.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.780
Is the answer sending thousands more troops
back to the country to just put it back in

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.290
the situation it was in before we even left?

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.420
That's also a terrible idea.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.310
Unfortunately.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.069
There's no easy answers.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:41.950
And any answer we have has to address the
fact that the United States has made this

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.540
situation so much worse.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.370
The Taliban now has their hands on all these
U.S. weapons that we've been sending over

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.260
there for decades now.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:58.140
They've got the strongholds, they have forced
us out, they have forced the Afghan government

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.760
out.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.250
And they say they're now waiting for a peaceful
transfer of power.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:13.880
So, again, I don't have a definitive answer,
one suggestion I have at this point.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.709
Is we need to do what George W. Bush originally
talked about doing until he pissed off all

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:22.130
our allies is we need a coalition.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.810
The United States has proven that we can't
handle the situation there, we never went

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.800
in with an actual strategy.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.849
So it's kind of hard 20 years after the fact,
to really be able to get a good, solid strategy,

00:04:34.849 --> 00:04:39.740
a really good ground game going because we
never had one to begin with.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:43.551
So everybody else that comes along, all the
other leaders, Obama, Trump and Biden, they're

00:04:43.551 --> 00:04:46.629
having to piece it together as they go.

00:04:46.629 --> 00:04:48.110
And nobody got it right.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:53.460
I mean, what's happening right now in Afghanistan
is proof that nobody got it right.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:05:00.689
The only difference is that for all of those
years, the Taliban really only had control

00:05:00.689 --> 00:05:01.689
on the outskirts.

00:05:01.689 --> 00:05:04.969
You know, the really rural areas of Afghanistan.

00:05:04.969 --> 00:05:08.650
That's that's where they were able to, you
know, see progress.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:12.370
That's where we were able to fight them back.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:17.020
And as soon as we leave, they come back.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:22.210
So the answer is not obviously sending more
troops over there for another 20 years, so

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:28.919
we have another generation of American soldiers
growing up as part of this war machine, that

00:05:28.919 --> 00:05:30.520
that's not that's not tenable.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.520
That's not something we can do.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:40.930
I do think the the best path forward at this
point, and again, I'm not a military strategist,

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:47.680
don't claim to be, but if we do not have a
solid coalition of allies, if we cannot get

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.150
other countries involved.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:52.610
To pledge.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:57.919
To protect this area, you know, if we have
to negotiate with the Taliban, then we have

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:01.520
to negotiate at this point.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.009
But honestly, I don't know what else.

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:10.860
And it all stems from those failures of the
war on terror.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:15.650
We have had Republicans try this, we have
had Democrats try this, this is now bipartisan

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:21.340
failure with regards to our Afghanistan foreign
policy.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:27.509
So the solution is not going to come from
the United States.

00:06:27.509 --> 00:06:31.169
We need people that are better at this, we
need people who can look at it a little more

00:06:31.169 --> 00:06:37.680
objectively than the United States can, because
we're still stuck in that war on terror mentality

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:41.050
that followed the attacks of 9/11.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:46.380
We're still not thinking clearly at this point,
and again, what's happening right now is further

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.460
proof of that.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:54.919
So if we can't get some cooler heads in there,
if we can't get some real, true allies, you

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:59.699
know, maybe other nations in the region, that
can help us out.

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:06.099
Then this is what it is and we're stuck with
this mess that we created.

00:07:06.099 --> 00:07:10.830
And in the meantime, until we figure this
out, the United States need to say, listen,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:14.610
we're going to take Afghan refugees.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:19.919
Over the weekend, tens of thousands of people
daily trying to get out of the country because

00:07:19.919 --> 00:07:24.490
they see what's happening, they understand
this is for real.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:30.559
OK, this isn't a temporary insurgency here
that we're seeing, this is what their life

00:07:30.559 --> 00:07:33.469
may become now.

00:07:33.469 --> 00:07:38.749
And I would say after 20 years of occupying
their country, after helping to destabilize

00:07:38.749 --> 00:07:42.670
it, I'd say that's the least we could do,
is take these people into our country.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:47.469
And that is the next step that I want to see
this Biden administration take.

00:07:47.469 --> 00:07:53.539
Acknowledge the failures of the United States,
acknowledge that we don't have the answers

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:57.080
yet, and that is a terrifying thing for a
country to admit.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.160
And I guarantee you you'll never hear them
say that.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.259
But at least we can do that.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:08.899
Me, everybody watching this, all of the other
people left and right out there with the armchair

00:08:08.899 --> 00:08:17.969
punditry admit that we don't know how to correctly
handle this situation.

00:08:17.969 --> 00:08:22.729
Because it sucks to have to admit that you
don't know it, but I think at this point that's

00:08:22.729 --> 00:08:26.689
where we're at and I don't think anybody can
definitively say that.

00:08:26.689 --> 00:08:31.289
Yes, we I know for certain we have to do this
or we can't do that.

00:08:31.289 --> 00:08:36.280
It's not that simple, but we're going to continue
to watch as the corporate media.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.340
CNN is already out there.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.729
The major newspapers are already out there.

00:08:38.729 --> 00:08:40.090
Oh, my God, this is horrible.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.241
We got to get troops back there.

00:08:41.241 --> 00:08:47.070
They're going to push for war because war
means ratings, war means advertisements, and

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.740
that's what makes them money.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:54.760
On the other side of all of this, you have
the Republicans out there nonstop over the

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.610
weekend telling us that this is a failure
of the Biden administration.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:03.930
This failure rests solely on his shoulders.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:08.560
And whether it's fair or not, it does.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.800
He is the leader of the country right now.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.640
This was a decision that was made.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:18.390
And so if it succeeds or fails, that is on
him.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.680
And you may think it's fair, you may think
it's not fair, but it doesn't matter, politically

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:26.400
speaking, yes, it is on him and Republicans
are going to do everything they can to use

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:30.990
that to their advantage, especially heading
into the midterms.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:36.890
As we all know, Republicans have struggled
terrifically, trying to come up with any kind

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:41.020
of talking point to take down Joe Biden.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.400
You know, going as far a couple of months
ago to blame him for the Chick fil A sauce

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:48.050
shortage.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:53.030
This is one that might stick and that's even
more terrifying, folks.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:57.750
Because of the midterm elections, and especially
if the twenty twenty four presidential elections

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:03.550
become about failed foreign policy and people
get mad at the Democrat who inherited all

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:04.550
of it.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:07.190
And again, I think it's rather unfair for
that to happen.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.790
But I understand that that is what is going
to happen.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.510
Then we're going to end up with something
terrible.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:17.720
That's a situation where you end up with somebody
like Tom Cotton coming out and saying, oh,

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.550
my God, we've got to get back over there.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.220
Look at all this instability the Democrats
created.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.010
The terrorists have taken over.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.690
I've been there.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:29.500
I know what it's like over there and I know
what we can do.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.660
And people will flock to that, I promise you.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:40.490
I can promise you that because we've seen
it happen, we saw it happen in the 2004 election.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:44.200
Turmoil in the Middle East.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:48.450
And the Republicans, unfortunately, did a
much better job of messaging, saying we're

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.900
the only ones that can keep you safe.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.010
They did it through misinformation, they did
it through lies, they did it through fake

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:56.730
news and all of that.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:59.980
Yes, but it worked on the American public.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:07.510
So twenty, twenty four could end up being
a repeat of the 2004 election based on that

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:10.940
simple fact.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.430
And again, that's the situation where you
end up with somebody worse, you end up with

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:21.060
the worst kind of warhawk at the top of that
Republican ticket, who is going to do unimaginable

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:25.380
things over there in the Middle East where
all of this is taking place, because it's

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.650
not just going to be about Afghanistan, either.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:30.280
They're going to throw in Iran.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:35.410
They're going to throw in Syria, they're going
to say, look at all these Democratic failures

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:39.610
abroad.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:40.860
That's bad news.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:46.810
That is bad news for the Democratic Party.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.950
And it's bad news for the United States as
well, and it's bad news for everybody over

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:55.120
there in the Middle East because, again, we
end up with somebody worse and I pick Tom

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:59.160
Cotton because he is somebody that served.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:04.790
This could be the kind of event that a guy
like him needs to really bolster up his poll

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.901
numbers, because trust me, he's not doing
well so far.

00:12:07.901 --> 00:12:11.160
And all the little straw polls for twenty,
twenty four.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:17.950
So this could be the moment that Tom Cotton
emerges as their guy, as the Republican's

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:18.950
guy.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:22.880
You know, Rhonda Santos doesn't have that,
Ted Cruz certainly doesn't have that, Donald

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.450
Trump obviously doesn't have that, although
he is going to try to use this to his advantage

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.460
as well.

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:36.190
But the point is, we can't go back to a situation,
whether it is with a Democrat or a Republican,

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:43.110
where we think that we can bomb our way out
of the problem, that's never going to work.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:46.340
We tried it for 20 years.

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:52.530
And an abrupt pull out here saying, well,
best of luck to you all, while it's best for

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:59.770
U.S. troops, sure, we've destabilize the region,
created hundreds of thousands of, you know,

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:06.950
evacuate refugees at this point, not just
evacuees, but refugees with nowhere to go.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:12.620
And we have to own that as a country, as an
administration, they have to own that.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.860
They may not have started this mess.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.830
But they've been with it every step of the
way, unfortunately.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:24.020
So we have to do better, we have to do better
for these people, we have to do better for

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:30.060
the world, and we have to get more people
on our side willing to take a leadership role,

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.910
take it away from us.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.530
I feel.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:37.430
And we can offer the support that they need.

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:41.730
I do not want another conflict in the Middle
East, I do not want more war, I do not want

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:46.060
more dead soldiers, whether it's U.S. soldiers
or whether it's a foreign country soldiers,

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:49.680
we don't need that at all.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:54.730
So we have to put our best and brightest together,
we got to get the intelligence and I don't

00:13:54.730 --> 00:14:00.290
mean like covert and I mean like literal intelligence,
the smart people in the room need to take

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:04.100
things over and they need to get with the
other smartest people around the country and

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:09.860
try to figure out a way that this doesn't
end with more bombs and more bloodshed.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:15.230
But unfortunately, I do not think that the
cooler heads are going to prevail in this

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:20.160
situation, and that is not going to end well
for anybody.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:15:28.650
I'm Ferrin Cousins in for David Pakman, we'll
be right back.

